course: dictionary
lesson: 5030
title: What an inhaler is
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inhaler is a small device you put in your mouth and press to breathe a medicine into your lungs. It is used mostly by people with asthma, a condition that can make breathing hard.
explain: Read the words around a new word to understand it. «Use your inhaler» tells you what people do with it. «Blue inhaler» and «reliever inhaler» name a kind of inhaler, and the sentences give clues about what each kind does.
explain: «A preventer inhaler contains a steroid that calms airway swelling over time and only works if taken every day.» The words "over time" and "every day" tell you a preventer is a medicine you take regularly, not one you grab in a rush.
fact: An inhaler is a small device you put in your mouth and press to breathe medicine into your lungs.
fact: Inhalers are used mostly for asthma.
fact: A reliever inhaler, often blue, opens narrowed airways during an attack.
fact: A preventer inhaler is taken every day and calms airway swelling over time.
fact: If someone has trouble breathing, tell an adult at once; if the inhaler does not help, an adult calls 999.
exercise: «Use your inhaler» appears in a health lesson. What is an inhaler? | A bag for your PE kit | A type of healthy snack | *A small device you press to breathe medicine into your lungs | A tiny torch for reading in bed
exercise: «A preventer inhaler ... only works if taken every day.» What does this tell you about a preventer inhaler? | It works once, the first time you use it | *It must be taken every day | It is only needed on sports day | It is a sweet treat
exercise: «Colds often trigger asthma.» Find and copy the word that means sets off. | *trigger | colds | asthma | often
test: «With their reliever inhaler, which opens narrowed airways, and an asthma plan, children with asthma can play almost any sport.» What does a reliever inhaler do? | *Opens narrowed airways | Makes you fall asleep | Keeps your bag dry | Cleans your teeth
test: In an asthma attack, what should you do first? | Give the inhaler to a friend to keep | Wait quietly and do nothing | Run around the playground to get warm | *Sit the person up, help them use their reliever inhaler and fetch an adult
exam: What does «a preventer inhaler» mean? | A type of school bag with a checklist | One that opens airways in seconds during an attack | A kind of pencil case for school | *One that calms airway swelling over time and is taken every day
